# Nellore Diwali Dhamaka — environment files
#
# The app reads a different file per Vite mode. There is no shared `.env`, so a
# production configuration can never leak into local development by accident.
#
#   .env.development   npm run dev            Firebase Emulator Suite (demo-* project)
#   .env.staging       npm run build:staging  staging Firebase project ("staging" alias)
#   .env.production    npm run build:prod     production Firebase project ("prod" alias)
#
# Copy the matching `*.example` file and fill it in. All real env files are
# git-ignored. VITE_* values end up in the public bundle: never place secrets,
# private keys or service-account credentials in them.
#
# Server-side settings (App Check enforcement) live in `functions/.env.<project-id>`
# — see functions/.env.example.
